# One line-ending convention. Without this every file saved on Windows looks
# fully rewritten and hides the real change in the diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep CRLF: cmd.exe mishandles LF around goto/labels, and
# WSH and PowerShell read CRLF more reliably.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.vbs  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.db   binary

# The README screenshot belongs to the GitHub page, not to the package the
# installer unpacks. git archive builds the release asset, so keep it out.
IMG/   export-ignore
